# Vendryx Admin Dashboard Configuration
#
# VITE_STHENO_BACKEND_URL must be LEFT EMPTY. vite.config.mts turns an empty
# value into a same-origin baseUrl, so the Medusa SDK requests this origin and
# the dev proxy forwards them with Host rewritten from the `stheno_tenant_host`
# cookie the tenant picker sets.
#
# Do not point it at http://127.0.0.1:9000. The engine resolves the merchant from
# the Host header, so an absolute URL makes every request arrive as ten_pro and
# Trial/Free fail with "Invalid credentials" no matter which dashboard is picked.
#
# The name must also be VITE_STHENO_BACKEND_URL, which is what vite.config.mts
# reads. It was previously VITE_STHENO_ADMIN_BACKEND_URL, read by nothing, so
# the config fell back to a hardcoded localhost:9000 that resolves to no tenant.
VITE_STHENO_BACKEND_URL=
VITE_STHENO_STOREFRONT_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Clerk Authentication for Storefront Owners
# Obtain from your Clerk Dashboard (https://dashboard.clerk.com -> API Keys)
#
# Left as pk_test_... on purpose: run-dev.bat comments this line out when it
# writes .env, because the placeholder is truthy and would override the working
# dev key built into clerk-auth-provider.tsx.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...